    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Really good at sticking its head in the sand. And so here is another issue where Congress is trying to stick its head in the sand. In Colorado alone, $2 billion of cash, you've got jobs are being created, but those employees can't take their money down to the bank and deposit it. They can't get a home loan if they're working in this industry. You've got families who, you know, this medical refugee situation where they're coming in from all over, especially early on in this, maybe less than now, with more and more states moving toward medical legalization. But they were coming to Colorado, separating their families, just to have access to the life-changing, life-saving pharmaceutical applications, the CBDs. And so you saw this happen, and yet, Washington's turning a blind eye to it. It's ignoring the issue and not fixing it.",
