    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94305.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so we had a group meeting, I think, gosh, I think we had maybe a dozen senators. One of the bigger meetings I've ever had here, when we try to get senators together for a meeting, they come in, they may eat the free food you have out on the table, and then they leave, and then somebody else comes in, and maybe they drink the free Pepsi you have at the table, and then they leave, and then trying to get a dozen or more in the room at the same time to stay for a while can be a trick. But we did. This meeting was probably the best attended, Republicans, Democrats, and we're sitting there trying to find a solution. You know, who's going to do what? You know, talking Ron Wyden and Kirsten Gillibrand was there and Maria Cantwell and Steve Danes and others were there. And, you know, Senator Warren talks about this, hey, you know, What about looking at this not from a standpoint of schedules or legalization, but looking at this from if a state has done it, letting the state do it. And that's kind of the genesis of how we move forward with it. And her saying that there was in line with what we had talked about the president with. So I may have gotten a little bit of the timeline out of order because that",
